{#
    Tabler Flag — a country, territory or organisation flag (`.flag .flag-country-{code}`),
    drawn at a 5:4 ratio. Needs Tabler's flags plugin: load `tabler-flags.css` (or
    `tabler-flags.min.css`) next to `tabler.css`.

    Usage:
        <twig:Tabler:Flag code="fr" label="France" />
        <twig:Tabler:Flag code="US" size="sm" />
        <twig:Tabler:Flag code="european-union" size="lg" label="European Union" />

    A flag is a picture: with `label`, it is an image named by it (role="img",
    aria-label); without, it is decoration hidden from assistive technology
    (aria-hidden="true"), for a flag next to the name in text.

    Props:
      code   — ISO 3166 code (`fr`, `us`, `gb-sct`…) or slug of a flag without one (`european-union`,
               `nato`); lowercased
      size   — xxs | xs | sm | md | lg | xl | 2xl (flag-{size}): the avatar sizes; unset, an avatar's
      label  — accessible name, e.g. the country name; unset, the flag is hidden from assistive technology
#}
{% apply trim %}
{% props
    ## string The ISO 3166 code, e.g. `fr` or `gb-sct`, or the slug of a flag without one, e.g. `european-union`; lowercased.
    code,
    ## 'xxs'|'xs'|'sm'|'md'|'lg'|'xl'|'2xl'|null The size, one of the avatar sizes (`flag-{size}`); unset, the size of an avatar.
    size = null,
    ## string|null The accessible name, e.g. the country name (`role="img"`, `aria-label`); unset, the flag is hidden from assistive technology.
    label = null,
%}

{% set flag = html_cva(
    base: 'flag',
    variants: {
        size: {
            xxs: 'flag-xxs',
            xs: 'flag-xs',
            sm: 'flag-sm',
            md: 'flag-md',
            lg: 'flag-lg',
            xl: 'flag-xl',
            '2xl': 'flag-2xl',
        },
    },
) %}

<span class="{{ flag.apply({size: size ?? ''}, 'flag-country-' ~ code|lower, attributes.render('class')) }}"
    {%- if label is not null %} role="img" aria-label="{{ label }}"{% else %} aria-hidden="true"{% endif %} {{ attributes.without('class') }}></span>
{% endapply ~%}
